From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:45:02 +0900
Subject: Input method: text from a nested host,
 and the on-screen keyboard only on internal outputs

InputMethod::commitHostText() gives text a nested backend's host committed (the Android
keyboard: Chinese, emoji, what no key can type) to the focused client's text input, or types
it with a temporary keymap when the client has none; the D-Bus commitText (next patch) uses it
too. KWIN_IM_SHOW_ALWAYS applies to text fields on internal outputs only: a field on an
external output (a TV the phone casts to, where the phone is the touchpad) does not pop up
the on-screen keyboard.

Split from the cast/host-text change (e07d7448) in the round-2 fold (docs/72).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [the internal-only rule may interest upstream; commitHostText serves the Android backend and D-Bus]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:input.text (host text through the Android backend); none for the TV rule (manual list)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/58 docs/60 docs/72
Origin: vendor
